# The resource server's one TLS-profile option.
#
# It is in a file of its own rather than interpolated in `compose.yaml` because
# `SSL_CERT_FILE=""` is not the same as unset. OpenSSL reads it as a filename —
# an empty one — and `ssl.create_default_context()` in the server image drops
# from 150 trusted authorities to nought when it is set that way. `httpx2`
# escapes that by testing the value for truth before using it, but the variable
# reaches every process in the container, and the default run has to be the run
# it always was.
#
# `keycloak/tls/keycloak.env` is the same mechanism for Keycloak's three, which
# fail louder: Quarkus refuses an empty value outright.

# The authority `generate.sh` minted, at the path `compose.yaml` mounts it. This
# is what makes ADR-0005's one-string rule survive the profile: the server is
# configured with the issuer and discovers the key set from it, so it has to be
# able to verify the name in that string.
SSL_CERT_FILE=/tls/authority.crt
